===Population estimates===
As of 2025, the population of Trinacria was estimated by [[Instituto Confederal de Stadística]] to have increased 11.4% from 2020 to 1,013,045 – Trinacria's estimated population represented 4.13% of the Metropolitan City's population of 24,479,594; 2.71% of the [[Concordia]] conurbation's population of 37,323,422; and 0.65% of Balisca's total population of 154,556,447. Also current to 2025, Trinacria's population consisted of 368,851 households, with 201,239 people living in group, [[w:Co-living|co-living]] quarters. The [[w:Population density|population density]] was 600 inhabitants per square kilometer (1,500/mi²). 

The cantonal Transportation and Housing Council noted that there was an abnormally negligible increase in population between 2015 and 2020. Areas with high proportions of immigrants and undocumented residents are traditionally undercounted for a variety of reasons, often based on a mistrust of cantonal officials or an unwillingness to be identified. In many cases, counts of vacant apartment units did not match data from communal surveys and reports from residents.

