{{bar percent|Other{{efn|Mostly [[Multiracial American]], other [[Asian Baliscans|Asian]] or other [[European Baliscans|European ancestry]]}}|gray|14.7}}}}In Trinacria, approximately 48.5% of the population was have origins outside of Castejón as of 2025. Of that, 42.5% were born in [[w:Latin America|Latin America]] (36.8% of which was from other regions of Balisca), 33.5% in [[W:Africa|Africa]], 11.8% in [[w:Europe|Europe]], 10.8% in [[W:Asia|Asia]], and 0.4% in [[w:North America|North America]]. Roughly 2.1% of the population was born abroad to Baliscan parents. Approximately 44.2% of the population over 5 years of age speak [[w:English language|English]] at home; 23.8% speak [[Baliscano language|Baliscano]] at home. Also, 16.8% of the populace speak other [[w:Indo-European languages|Indo-European languages]] at home. Another 13.5% speak an [[w:Languages of Asia|Asian language]] at home.

Among the Asian population, people of [[w:Chinese diaspora|Chinese ethnicity]] make up the largest ethnic group at 10.2% of Trinacria's population, with about 94,200 people; the other East and Southeast Asian groups are: [[Okataian Baliscans|Okataian]]s (5.3%), [[Korean Baliscans|Korean]]s (2.9%), [[Filipino Baliscans|Filipino]]s (1.7%), [[Japanese Baliscans|Japanese]] (0.3%), [[Thai Baliscans|Thai]]s (0.2%), [[Vietnamese Baliscan|Vietnamese]] (0.2%), and [[Indonesian Baliscans|Indonesian]]s and [[Burmese Baliscans|Burmese]] both make up 0.1% of the population. People of [[w:South Asian|South Asian]] descent make up 7.8% of Trinacria's population: [[Indian Baliscans|Indians]] (5.3%), [[Bangladeshi Baliscans|Bangladeshi]] (1.5%), [[Pakistani Baliscans|Pakistani]]s (0.7%), and [[Nepalese Baliscans|Nepali]] (0.2%).

Among the Ibero-Baliscan population, [[Iberians]] make up the largest ethnic group at 4.9%, next to [[Mexican Baliscans|Mexican]]s, who make up 4.2% of the population, and [[Dominican Baliscans|Dominican]]s at 3.9%. [[w:Puerto Rican people|Puerto Rican]]s make up 2.4%. [[w:South America|South American]]s constitute 9.6% of Trinacria's population, mainly of [[Brazilian Baliscans|Brazilians]] (4.4%) and [[Venezuelan Baliscans|Venezuelan]] descent (3.2%).
